                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c92cb8aa-df14-423f-93ed-cc7c29d43c39",
                                "sense_id": "8cb59511-34a4-3a68-99d0-5be0e8f8bef8",
                                "text": "At one time were bison on the American plains not merely abundant but superabundant: they seemed inexhaustible."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6db63386-c2bb-43a6-9238-34da8c3dd368",
                                "sense_id": "8cb59511-34a4-3a68-99d0-5be0e8f8bef8",
                                "text": "Cornead. The ſpirit of foolery out of this Archibald Rupenrope he ſhall never be able to caſt, were the nectar of his eloquence a thouſand times more ſuperabundant, inceſſant ſourding."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
